From 630283cf5bf72f21cefe05286919aa312dce8340 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 07:13:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: preserve filesystem quoting on the consumer with raw
 string fields

Add the explicit message-only :fsq formatter for copied/static STRING
snapshots. It exactly follows fs::quoted's double quote delimiter and
ampersand escape character, preserving embedded quotes, ampersands,
backslashes and byte values. Structured encoders retain the original
unquoted value. Unsupported runtime field kinds keep their placeholder;
production lint requires a STRING key.

The reviewed AST converter permits :fsq only when the old %s argument is
an exact fs::quoted(...) call. Ordinary string arguments cannot acquire
new quoting silently. This does not change snapshot storage, ring/drop
policy, event severity, encoder fields or producer-side PathToString.

Native fixtures compare message bytes against the actual fs::quoted
helper and JSON values against snapshots after producer mutation, with
empty, quote/escape, whitespace, UTF8, embedded NUL and static strings.
Converter and lint fixtures also reject wrong types and unrelated quoted
functions. These test/support edits are reviewed code, not mass codemods.

Source checks: converter16 fixtures, lint13 contract tests, production
lint307 and whitespace pass. Actual native before/after consumer probes
and Logger test execution are pending separate resource-coordinated gates;
no runtime or performance pass is claimed from these source checks.
Shared eCash API; V2 inherits unchanged.
